![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Swallowing the error in the `catch` block without logging it on the server makes it difficult to diagnose network-level failures (e.g., DNS issues, timeouts, or connection resets). While returning a structured 502 to the client is an improvement, the underlying cause should be logged for server-side observability.

```suggestion
	} catch (error) {
		console.error('Image generation fetch failed:', error);
		return buildError(502, 'IMAGE_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE', 'Image generation service is unavailable.');
	}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Removing the `console.error` entirely removes all observability for failures in `getStudioTextAction`. If the concern is leaking internal state to the browser console, consider logging a sanitized message. Without any log, debugging issues where an `actionId` might be misconfigured or missing becomes significantly harder.

```
		} catch {
			console.error('Studio text action lookup failed');
			textError = 'This action is not available. Try Generate Verdict instead.';
			return;
		}
```
